meta {
  name: Print Data
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{PRIVATE_BASE_URL}}/api/v1/admin/orders/print-data
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "ids": ["{{ORDER_ID}}"]
  }
}

docs {
  # POST /api/v1/admin/orders/print-data

  Editor or superadmin. Returns invoice fields for the ids that exist. Missing ids are listed and are not a 404. This does not mark the order printed.

  Each order includes `invoice_id` (`INV-` plus the order number's hex body), `number`, `order_number`, `created_at`, `estimated_delivery_date` (computed, not stored), `customer_name`, `phone`, `email` (empty when none), `full_address`, `courier_name`, `tracking_number`, and items with `title`, `variant_label`, `sku`, `product_id_short`, `quantity`, `unit_price`, `line_total`. Totals are the stored totals.

  Mark printed with POST /api/v1/admin/orders/printed and the same body. A reprint is allowed and each print is written to the activity log. `printed_at` is the latest time.

  Ready to pack is GET /api/v1/admin/orders/ready-to-pack (confirmed orders). POST bulk-status with `packed` moves them on.
}
